---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { methods } from "../../data/api";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
const python = `import json, os, socket

request = {
    "method": "appearance",
    "value": json.dumps({"accent": "#c4b5fd", "gap": 16})
}
with socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX) as client:
    client.settimeout(3)
    client.connect(os.environ["LUDASH_CONTROL"])
    client.sendall(json.dumps(request).encode() + b"\\n")
    data = b""
    while b"\\n" not in data:
        chunk = client.recv(65536)
        if not chunk or len(data) + len(chunk) > 1024 * 1024:
            raise RuntimeError("Invalid LunaDash response")
        data += chunk
    response = json.loads(data)
    if "error" in response:
        raise RuntimeError(response["error"])
    print(response["appearance"])`;
---
<DocsLayout title="Talk to your desktop." section="api" summary="Use the local control socket, write a Quickshell component, or build an opt-in native effect. Each interface has a different scope and trust boundary.">
  <nav class="doc-toc" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#ipc">Local IPC</a><a href="#methods">Methods</a><a href="#qml">QML interface</a><a href="#native">Native plugins</a></nav>
  <div class="doc-callout"><p><strong>This is a local API, not an HTTP service.</strong> The website documents and previews configuration; it does not control your desktop. The compositor's Unix socket is restricted to the session user.</p></div>
  <h2 id="ipc">Start with ludashctl</h2><p>Applications launched inside LunaDash inherit <code>LUDASH_CONTROL</code>. For an external terminal, point it at your running session's socket. The default session name is <code>ludash-0</code>; substitute the name passed to <code>--socket</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={'export LUDASH_CONTROL="$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ludash-test-control"\n./build/ludashctl status\n./build/ludashctl appearance \'{"gap":16,"animations":true}\'\n./build/ludashctl open-settings modules'} />
  <p>Send one UTF-8 JSON object followed by a newline. <code>method</code> and <code>value</code> are strings; JSON-valued settings are encoded inside <code>value</code>. Numeric IDs are also sent as strings.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="WIRE REQUEST" code={'{"method":"appearance","value":"{\\"gap\\":16}"}\n'} />
  <p>A successful call generally returns an updated state object. Failure returns <code>{'{"error":"message"}'}</code>; the CLI exits nonzero. Audio and power helpers run asynchronously, so acceptance is not completion—poll status for busy/error fields. Requests are limited to 64 KiB with a three-second server deadline; a client should also bound response size and time.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="PYTHON / DIRECT SOCKET CLIENT" code={python} />
  <h2 id="methods">Control methods</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Value</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{methods.map(method => <tr><td class="api-method">{method.name}</td><td>{method.value}</td><td>{method.behavior}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <h2 id="qml">A small QML interface</h2><p>SDK 2 visual plugins receive <code>shell</code>, validated <code>settings</code> and a feature-specific <code>context</code>. Legacy custom modules receive <code>shell</code>, resolved <code>style</code> and <code>moduleId</code>. Read <code>shell.state</code> as a snapshot and use commands for changes. The host manages the window, dimensions, animation and fallback content.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="QML / COMMON CALLS" code={'shell.launch("terminal")\nshell.launch("files")\nshell.command("workspace", 1)\nshell.setAppearance({ blur: true, blurRadius: 18 })\nshell.settingsOpen = true\nconst title = shell.focusedTitle\nconst label = shell.tr("Settings")'} />
  <p><a href={`${base}docs/modules/`}>The component guide</a> includes a complete Item template, JSON styles and recovery steps. Custom QML can execute processes and access files; metadata does not isolate it.</p>
  <h2 id="native">Plugin SDK 2 · live hooks</h2>
  <p>Choose <code>effect</code> for C/C++ hooks, <code>quickshell</code> for QML content, or <code>opengl</code> for vertex/fragment shader packages. Metadata selects a registered <code>target</code> and <code>replace</code> or <code>augment</code> mode. Every package uses the LunaDash CMake SDK; native code remains disabled until explicitly enabled.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="CREATE / BUILD / INSTALL" code={'lunadash-create-plugin --type effect --target window-animation --id org.example.motion --output my-motion\ncmake -S my-motion -B my-motion/build -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX="$HOME/.local"\ncmake --build my-motion/build\ncmake --install my-motion/build\nludashctl open-settings modules'} />
  <p>Native hooks receive JSON containing <code>target</code>, <code>mode</code>, <code>context</code>, <code>builtin</code>, <code>current</code> and <code>settings</code>. Implement <code>ludash_plugin_process</code> and return a validated JSON response. The SDK provides the entry point, embeds the manifest and creates a build receipt. Hooks cover window layout, initial window rules, window animation profiles and shell animation duration.</p>
  <p>Enabling, disabling, updating settings and rebuilding a package apply without rebooting or logging out. The host checks packages approximately once per second and stages each revision privately before reloading between calls. Hooks must be synchronous: do not retain host pointers, start background threads or register callbacks that outlive a call. Errors restore the built-in feature, and the Modules page remains available for recovery.</p>
  <p>OpenGL packages compile <code>.vert</code> and <code>.frag</code> with Qt Shader Tools. Their shaders operate on Quickshell visual slots; application buffers and the compositor output framebuffer are outside this SDK. Software rendering retains the original visual.</p>
  <div class="doc-callout"><p><strong>Native code runs inside the compositor.</strong> Metadata and build receipts are not a sandbox or signature. A faulty native plugin can crash or hang the session. LunaDash does not load KWin plugins or implement KWin's ABI.</p></div>
  <p>Start with the <a href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LunaDash/tree/dev/examples/plugins/stacking-windows">stacking-window example</a> for conventional overlapping windows, or use the four C, C++, Quickshell and OpenGL templates. See the <a href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LunaDash/blob/dev/docs/PLUGINS.md">SDK guide</a> and <a href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LunaDash/blob/dev/docs/PLUGIN_TARGETS.md">complete target and hook reference</a> for contracts and settings.</p>
</DocsLayout>
